Z||000000||Seanh||11-21-2000||11:24 PM||||Thats right, V7. She broke a rod yesterday, but only one, and is still running on 7 cylinders. It has 266K on her, so it was about time for a Ford. I am going to work on it tomarrow and get the piston out before it decides to fall into the crank. I dont know how it broke yet, but I am guessing the cap broke, but I wont be for sure untill tomarrow. I just think it is strange, as I have never heard of somthing like this happening. Oh well, its a Ford, anything is possible.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||11-22-2000||07:05 AM||||Happens all the time. Threw a rod in my Merc V6 outboard once, came in from 20 mi off shore on 5 cyl. Boy was that noisy with that big hole in the block.||||reg||1
